  "content": {
    "id": "p8-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "Find the value(s) of $k$ if the quadratic equation $x^2-(k+2)x+k+1=0$ has:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p8-q9-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Equal roots",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$k=0$",
          "worked": "For equal roots, $\\alpha=\\beta=r$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}2r&=k+2\\\\r^2&=k+1\\\\\\left(\\frac{k+2}{2}\\right)^2&=k+1\\\\k^2+4k+4&=4k+4\\\\k&=0\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 29
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q9-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "One root equal to $5$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$k=4$",
          "worked": "Let the other root be $\\beta$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}5+\\beta&=k+2\\\\\\beta&=k-3\\\\5\\beta&=k+1\\\\5(k-3)&=k+1\\\\4k&=16\\\\k&=4\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 29
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q9-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Consecutive roots",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$k=\\pm1$",
          "worked": "Let the roots be $r$ and $r+1$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}r+(r+1)&=k+2\\\\r&=\\frac{k+1}{2}\\\\r(r+1)&=k+1\\\\\\frac{(k+1)(k+3)}4&=k+1\\\\k^2+4k+3&=4k+4\\\\k^2&=1\\\\k&=\\pm1\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q9-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "One root double the other",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$k=-\\dfrac12,\\ 1$",
          "worked": "Let the roots be $r$ and $2r$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}3r&=k+2\\\\r&=\\frac{k+2}{3}\\\\2r^2&=k+1\\\\2\\left(\\frac{k+2}{3}\\right)^2&=k+1\\\\2k^2+8k+8&=9k+9\\\\2k^2-k-1&=0\\\\(2k+1)(k-1)&=0\\\\k&=-\\frac12\\text{ or }1\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q9-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "Reciprocal roots",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$k=0$",
          "worked": "Reciprocal roots have product $1$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\alpha\\beta&=k+1\\\\1&=k+1\\\\k&=0\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      }
    ]
  },
